Spotify Connect plugin for Kalinka
=================================

This package installs the Python wheel under /opt/kalinka/wheels and the
patched librespot 0.8.0 executable, built for this architecture, at
/usr/libexec/kalinka-plugin-spotify/librespot. The kalinka-server-restart
dpkg trigger asks the server to restart; Kalinka's bootstrap then installs the
wheel into its managed environment. The plugin is disabled by default.

Before enabling Spotify:

* Install the matching SDK 3.5, server and renderer streaming support described
  in docs/core-compatibility.md in the source repository. SDK 3.5 alone is not
  sufficient; the server and renderer must support unfinished HTTP streams.
* Spotify's executable setting defaults to the bundled librespot. A stock
  librespot executable is incompatible; point the setting elsewhere only at
  another build of this repository's patch.
* Select a renderer through Kalinka, enable Spotify Connect, and pair using
  the Spotify app with a Premium account.

Removal uninstalls the plugin from /opt/kalinka/venv using Kalinka's standard
prerm hook. Upgrades leave the existing installation in place until bootstrap
installs the new wheel. The package does not delete account credentials or
configuration, and it does not install a separate Spotify systemd service.
The plugin supervises its owned librespot process and restarts it after an
unexpected exit, with retry delays capped at 30 seconds (five minutes while
Spotify refuses sign-in). Disabling the plugin
or shutting down the server cancels retries. An interrupted Spotify session
may need selecting Kalinka and pressing Play again after discovery returns.

Build and operation instructions:
https://github.com/Kalinka-Player/kalinka-plugin-spotify
